│ # RTEC Syntax Reference                                                                                                                                                                                                           │
│                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   │
│ ## Overview                                                                                                                                                                                                                       │
│                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   │
│ The Event Calculus is a logic-based formalism for representing and reasoning about events and their effects. The Run-Time Event Calculus (RTEC) is a Prolog programming implementation of the Event Calculus, that has been       │
│ optimised for composite activity recognition. Below, we summarise the language of RTEC.                                                                                                                                           │
│                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   │
│ Following the Prolog convention, variables start with an upper-case letter, while predicates and constants start with a lower-case letter. Each rule ends with a full-stop “.”, while the head of a rule is separated from its    │
│ body with “:-”.                                                                                                                                                                                                                   │
│                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   │
│ A fluent is a property that may have different values at different points in time. The term F=V denotes that fluent F has value V.  Boolean fluents are a special case in which the possible values are “true” and “false”.       │
│                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   │
│ ## RTEC predicates                                                                                                                                                                                                                │
│ Below are the predicates of RTEC.                                                                                                                                                                                                 │
│                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   │
│ RTEC - Predicate 1: happensAt(E,T)                                                                                                                                                                                                │
│ Meaning: Event E occurs at time T                                                                                                                                                                                                 │
│                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   │
│ RTEC - Predicate 2: holdsAt(F=V,T)                                                                                                                                                                                                │
│ Meaning: The value of fluent F                                                                                                                                                                                                    │
